nd\n     Amgen cut prices faster than assumed; biosimilar margin collapsed; capacity was\n     underutilized. \u2192 Early warning: q/q gross margin compression in biosimilar segment\n     and price disclosures from competitors.\n  2. \"Pfizer/Metsera's GLP-1 program failed or was deprioritized.\" The manufacturing\n     contract never generated volume; the India facilities sat idle, saddling the balance\n     sheet with underabsorbed overhead. \u2192 Early warning: Pfizer GLP-1 clinical readouts\n     (expected 2027\u20132028), contract manufacturing order announcements.\n  3. \"The capital structure broke.\" A generic pricing shock plus a failed Kashiv\n     integration caused OCF to fall below interest and capex, forcing an equity raise at\n     $5\u20137/share. \u2192 Early warning: net leverage > 5x, interest coverage < 1.5x, liquidity\n     covenant breach, or guidance withdrawal.\n\nDecision Journal Entry (T0 2026-08-24):\n\n  Price: $17.91, IV: \u2248 $20.00 (base), MoS: \u2248 10%.\n  Key assumptions: FY2026E EBITDA $765M, FY2030E revenue $4.05B / EBITDA margin 25.9%,\n  WACC 9.6%, terminal growth 3%.\n  Red Team concern: The market is paying for the bull case; the equity story is priced\n  for flawless execution. The best entries historically were at $9\u201311; I am buying\n  momentum at 93% of the 52-week high, not value.\n  Risk caps: max 4% weight, hard stop/re-evaluation if thesis integrity triggers breach.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 LAYER 9. RED TEAM & ADVERS